        "translation": "Cessation means a state of happiness in which suffering has ended.\n\nEven describing it as a happy state in which suffering ends is strained language. The Buddha’s Truth of Cessation cannot truly be explained in words. We cannot imagine the greatness of the Dharma. Why, for this aim of the Truth of Cessation—the complete ending of suffering—must people relinquish every worldly happiness? Because, according to the Buddha, correctly practicing the Noble Eightfold Path leads us to where suffering is no more.",
