        "translation": "By the Buddha’s stated standard, after Right Mindfulness with lucid awareness has been attained for a time, practitioners eliminate the five hindrances in preparation for entering the First Jhāna. This is an indispensable stage and a precise measure of practice. If we experience unusual spiritual states but still retain the five hindrances, those strange states are not evidence of progress in the right direction; they may be temporary illusions. Eliminating the hindrances involves morality—sensual desire and ill will—wisdom—uncertainty—and capacity—sloth and restlessness.",
